cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the InsureDial dataset, please cite the paper below."
title: "PersuaRL: Reinforcement Learning-Driven Multi-Expert Selection for Persuasive Dialogue Generation in Insurance"
abstract: >-
  PersuaRL is a reinforcement learning framework that equips LLM-driven dialogue
  agents with the ability to adaptively explore, select and coordinate across
  multiple expert modules, guided by the evolving dialogue context, to achieve
  more effective persuasion. It is accompanied by InsureDial, a persuasive motor
  insurance dialogue dataset annotated for persuasion strategy, user intent,
  sentiment and key domain terms.
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous ACL submission"
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - persuasive dialogue
  - large language models
  - GRPO
  - multi-expert systems
